      "signal": "RoadCurv_1pm",
      "source_spec": "dev-planning/acc-plant-mf4/spec.md (rev 2)",
      "table": "acc_pt_can_100hz",
      "unit": "1/m"
    },
    {
      "channel_group": "PT_CAN_100Hz",
      "column_type": "double",
      "dtype": "float32",
      "enum_map": null,
      "notes": "ACHIEVED ego longitudinal acceleration (ESP), including road load. A plant output: never clipped by the limiter chain (spec 2.6 item 6). Differentiate this channel for jerk; jerk itself is deliberately not emitted. MF4 unit string: 'm/s²'; published ASCII-canonicalised.",
      "quantisation": null,
      "raster_hz": 100,
      "role": "response",
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "signal": "VehAccel_mps2",
      "source_spec": "dev-planning/acc-plant-mf4/spec.md (rev 2)",
      "table": "acc_pt_can_100hz",
      "unit": "m/s^2"
    },
    {
      "channel_group": "PT_CAN_100Hz",
      "column_type": "double",
      "dtype": "float32",
      "enum_map": null,
      "notes": "Lateral acceleration, v_e^2 * kappa. Kinematic consequence of the prescribed road curvature, not a dynamic response. There is no bicycle model, no tyre model and no lateral limiter behind it; see spec 1.7.1. Not sufficient for any lateral-dynamics requirement. Unbounded by grip: it may exceed what a real vehicle could sustain, and that is not a defect. MF4 unit string: 'm/s²'; published ASCII-canonicalised.",
      "quantisation": null,
      "raster_hz": 100,
      "role": "diagnostic",
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "signal": "VehLatAccel_mps2",
      "source_spec": "dev-planning/acc-plant-mf4/spec.md (rev 2)",
      "table": "acc_pt_can_100hz",
      "unit": "m/s^2"
    },
    {
      "channel_group": "PT_CAN_100Hz",
      "column_type": "double",
      "dtype": "float32",
      "enum_map": null,
      "notes": "Ego longitudinal speed, wheel-speed-decoded, quantised to sensor.quantisation.vehspd_kph. Not delayed by the sensor latency: this is a chassis signal, not a radar measurement.",
      "quantisation": 0.01,
      "raster_hz": 100,
      "role": "response",
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "signal": "VehSpd_Kph",
      "source_spec": "dev-planning/acc-plant-mf4/spec.md (rev 2)",
      "table": "acc_pt_can_100hz",
      "unit": "km/h"
    },
    {
      "channel_group": "PT_CAN_100Hz",
      "column_type": "int32",
      "dtype": "uint8",
      "enum_map": null,
      "notes": "Standstill indication, 0/1, asserted below hold.v_standstill_eps_mps -- the project-wide standstill definition. MF4 unit string: ''; published ASCII-canonicalised.",
      "quantisation": null,
      "raster_hz": 100,
      "role": "response",
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "signal": "VehStandstill_Flg",
      "source_spec": "dev-planning/acc-plant-mf4/spec.md (rev 2)",
      "table": "acc_pt_can_100hz",
      "unit": "1"
    },
    {
      "channel_group": "PT_CAN_100Hz",
      "column_type": "double",
      "dtype": "float32",
      "enum_map": null,
      "notes": "Yaw rate, v_e * kappa. Kinematic consequence of the prescribed road curvature, not a dynamic response. There is no bicycle model, no tyre model and no lateral limiter behind it; see spec 1.7.1. Not sufficient for any lateral-dynamics requirement.",
      "quantisation": null,
      "raster_hz": 100,
      "role": "diagnostic",
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "signal": "VehYawRate_dps",
      "source_spec": "dev-planning/acc-plant-mf4/spec.md (rev 2)",
      "table": "acc_pt_can_100hz",
      "unit": "deg/s"
    },
    {
      "channel_group": "RADAR_OBJ_50Hz",
      "column_type": "double",
      "dtype": "float32",
      "enum_map": null,
      "notes": "Bearing to the tracked object in slot Obj2, atan2(y_cart, x_long), quantised to sensor.quantisation.azimuth_deg. Range plus azimuth is what makes two objects discriminable (ISO 15622:2018 clause 7.5).",
      "quantisation": 0.1,
      "raster_hz": 50,
      "role": "response",
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "signal": "Obj2_Azimuth_deg",
      "source_spec": "dev-planning/acc-plant-mf4/spec.md (rev 2)",
      "table": "acc_radar_obj_50hz",
      "unit": "deg"
    },
    {
      "channel_group": "RADAR_OBJ_50Hz",
      "column_type": "double",
      "dtype": "float32",
      "enum_map": null,
      "notes": "Longitudinal range to the tracked object in slot Obj2, arc length, bumper to bumper. Quantised to sensor.quantisation.dist_m. Negative values mean the bodies have interpenetrated: there is no collision detection in the plant.",
      "quantisation": 0.05,
      "raster_hz": 50,
      "role": "response",
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "signal": "Obj2_Dist_m",
      "source_spec": "dev-planning/acc-plant-mf4/spec.md (rev 2)",
      "table": "acc_radar_obj_50hz",
      "unit": "m"
    },
    {
      "channel_group": "RADAR_OBJ_50Hz",
      "column_type": "int32",
      "dtype": "uint16",
      "enum_map": null,
      "notes": "Track ID of the tracked object in slot Obj2; 0 when the slot is empty. Stable for the life of the track, so a change of Trgt_ID always means a reselection. MF4 unit string: ''; published ASCII-canonicalised.",
      "quantisation": null,
      "raster_hz": 50,
      "role": "response",
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "signal": "Obj2_ID",
      "source_spec": "dev-planning/acc-plant-mf4/spec.md (rev 2)",
      "table": "acc_radar_obj_50hz",
      "unit": "1"
    },
    {
      "channel_group": "RADAR_OBJ_50Hz",
      "column_type": "int32",
      "dtype": "uint8",
      "enum_map": null,
      "notes": "Same-lane classification of the tracked object in slot Obj2 after curve compensation and the confirm/drop hysteresis. This is the sensor's own answer; a curve target-selection check should recompute it from LatOfs and RoadCurv. MF4 unit string: ''; published ASCII-canonicalised.",
      "quantisation": null,
      "raster_hz": 50,
      "role": "response",
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "signal": "Obj2_InLane_Flg",
      "source_spec": "dev-planning/acc-plant-mf4/spec.md (rev 2)",
      "table": "acc_radar_obj_50hz",
      "unit": "1"
    },
    {
      "channel_group": "RADAR_OBJ_50Hz",
      "column_type": "double",
      "dtype": "float32",
      "enum_map": null,
      "notes": "CARTESIAN (sensor-frame) lateral offset of the tracked object in slot Obj2. Combine with RoadCurv_1pm to recompute the path-relative offset y_path = y_cart - 0.5*kappa*x^2 (spec 1.5.7). The path-relative offset is deliberately not emitted.",
      "quantisation": null,
      "raster_hz": 50,
      "role": "response",
